@startuml GitEasyModuleDependency
title GitEasy - Module Dependencies (v1.5.5)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "GitEasy" {
  component "GitEasy.psd1\nGitEasy.psm1\n21 public + 21 private functions" as Core
}

package "Hard runtime dependency\n(absent = module fails)" {
  component "git.exe\n(any recent version)" <<boundary>> as Git
}

package "Soft runtime dependencies\n(absent = reduced function, not crash)" {
  component "git-credential-manager (GCM)\nor compatible credential helper" <<boundary>> as GCM
  component "cmdkey.exe\n(Windows Credential Manager)" <<boundary>> as Cmdkey
  component "SSH agent + key pair\n(for SSH remotes)" <<boundary>> as SSH
}

package "External services\n(reached through git.exe)" {
  component "GitHub / GitLab\nor any HTTPS/SSH Git remote" <<boundary>> as Remote
}

package "Development dependencies\n(tests only; not shipped)" {
  component "Pester 3+ (PS 5.1)\nor Pester 5+ (PS 7)" <<helper>> as Pester
  component "PSScriptAnalyzer" <<helper>> as PSSA
}

Core --> Git : all git calls route\nthrough Invoke-GEGit (single seam)
Core --> GCM : Set-Vault writes helper config;\nReset-Login erases stored entry
Core --> Cmdkey : Reset-Login only (best-effort;\nWindows; failure non-fatal)
Core --> SSH : Set-Ssh writes SSH remote URL;\ngit.exe handles key auth from there
Core --> Remote : through git.exe (fetch / push)

Pester ..> Core : imports for testing
PSSA ..> Core : lints at build time

note bottom of Core
  Module imports nothing at runtime.\ngit.exe is the only hard dep.\nAll other deps are opt-in paths.
end note
@enduml
